  <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl font-light text-charcoal mb-6">Tools for Makers</h1>

  <p class="font-body text-charcoal/70 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
    Technology as an extension of craft.
  </p>
  <p class="font-body text-charcoal/70 leading-relaxed mb-16">
    The best tools disappear into the work — leaving the judgment, the touch, and the making entirely to you.
  </p>

  <div class="border-t border-ash pt-12">

    {# Tool card: Carver's Pattern Maker #}
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-12 items-start mb-16">
      {# App icon — squircle is baked into the PNG, so no CSS radius here #}
      <a href="{{ '/pattern_maker/' | url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="shrink-0">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/images/tools/pattern-maker-icon.png' | url }}"
             alt="Carver's Pattern Maker app icon"
             width="512" height="512" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             class="w-20 h-20 md:w-28 md:h-28">
      </a>
      <div class="flex-1">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-light text-charcoal mb-2">Carver's Pattern Maker</h2>
        <p class="font-ui text-[11px] tracking-widest uppercase text-charcoal/40 mb-4">Wood carving</p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/70 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Turn a photograph of a spoon, bowl, or other carvable object into a pattern you can print at true scale. <strong class="font-normal text-charcoal">Nothing to install — open Pattern Maker in Safari, Chrome, or Firefox and start working.</strong> The object is traced for you; set the finished size, then add centerlines, grids, and layout lines to help transfer the shape to your blank. Use top and side photographs together and they print with shared registration marks so the two views stay aligned in the shop.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/60 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Your photographs never leave your device. There are no accounts, subscriptions, locked features, or tracking.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/60 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong class="font-normal text-charcoal/80">Pattern Maker is completely free, supported by optional contributions from the woodworkers who find it useful.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/50 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Safari, Chrome, and Firefox are supported.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
          <a href="{{ '/pattern_maker/' | url }}"
             class="inline-block font-ui text-xs tracking-widest uppercase border border-charcoal text-charcoal px-8 py-3 hover:bg-charcoal hover:text-ground transition-colors text-center"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Open Pattern Maker →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# Tool card: Bowl Designer #}
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-12 items-start">
      {# App icon — square source, so the macOS squircle is applied in CSS to match the Pattern Maker #}
      <a href="{{ '/bowl_designer/' | url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="shrink-0">
        <img src="{{ '/assets/images/tools/bowl-designer-icon.png' | url }}"
             alt="Bowl Designer app icon"
             width="512" height="512" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             class="w-20 h-20 md:w-28 md:h-28 rounded-[22%]">
      </a>
      <div class="flex-1">
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-light text-charcoal mb-2">Bowl Designer</h2>
        <p class="font-ui text-[11px] tracking-widest uppercase text-charcoal/40 mb-4">Bowl turning</p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/70 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Design a bowl before you commit wood to it. <strong class="font-normal text-charcoal">Nothing to install — open Bowl Designer in Safari, Chrome, or Firefox and start designing.</strong> Shape the profile visually, adjust dimensions and proportions, choose species, and see the finished form as you work. Build a solid turned bowl or design a segmented one ring by ring, down to individual segments, feature rings, and mosaic patterns.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/70 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Because it runs entirely in the browser, <strong class="font-normal text-charcoal">clients can use it too</strong>. Send a design to a client to review, or let a client open Bowl Designer, create what they have in mind, and send the design to you to refine and build. No software installation or account stands between them and the design.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/70 leading-relaxed mb-6">
          When it is time to build, Bowl Designer turns the design into shop information: cut lists, bills of materials, stock dimensions, and <strong class="font-normal text-charcoal">true-scale construction templates</strong>. Print the turned profile at actual size to transfer important locations and curves to the blank and use it as a reference while shaping. For segmented work, true-scale segment contours let you make <strong class="font-normal text-charcoal">one test cut and check its dimensions and angles against the printed pattern before cutting the rest.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/60 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          Your designs stay on your device unless you choose to share them. There are no accounts, subscriptions, locked features, or tracking.
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/60 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
          <strong class="font-normal text-charcoal/80">Bowl Designer is completely free to use and to share, supported by optional contributions from the woodworkers who find it useful.</strong>
        </p>
        <p class="font-body text-charcoal/50 text-sm leading-relaxed mb-8">
          Safari, Chrome, and Firefox are supported.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3">
          <a href="{{ '/bowl_designer/' | url }}"
             class="inline-block font-ui text-xs tracking-widest uppercase border border-charcoal text-charcoal px-8 py-3 hover:bg-charcoal hover:text-ground transition-colors text-center"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            Open Bowl Designer →
          </a>
          <a href="https://justwood.design/bowl_designer/"
             class="inline-block font-ui text-xs tracking-widest uppercase text-charcoal/50 px-8 py-3 hover:text-charcoal transition-colors text-center hidden">
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

